  "report": {
    "incident_title": "Card payments failing with 'Payment method could not be verified'",
    "outcome": "conclusive",
    "summary": "Card payments fail because payments-svc pods are still using the PSP API key pk_live_..A7, which was revoked at the PSP at 07:00:30Z by the automated rotate-psp-keys job. The job replaced it with pk_live_..C2 at 06:58Z and was configured with revoke_previous_immediately=true, so there was no overlap window. Pods that still hold A7 get 401 invalid_api_key from the PSP, which payments-svc maps to PAYMENT_METHOD_UNVERIFIED. The one pod that loaded C2 (created by an HPA scale-up at 09:08Z) authorizes successfully. UPI and wallets run on a separate provider and are unaffected. The card form deploy (web-frontend v8.2.0, 06:45Z) is not the cause: card errors begin after the key revocation, not at the deploy. The failure is not visible in 5xx or healthz metrics, which is why the dashboard looks healthy.",
    "root_cause": "Automated PSP key rotation (vault rotate-psp-keys, configured 2026-05-25 with revoke_previous_immediately=true) revoked the previous live key pk_live_..A7 at the PSP at 07:00:30Z while payments-svc pods were still running with it. Pods did not reload the new key pk_live_..C2 from vault, so their PSP authorize calls were rejected with 401 invalid_api_key.",
    "confidence": "high",
